A3-Q-SCALING  --  Q(inf) = int_0^inf q(t) dt under a -> 0
model 1 (single link SU(2), exact): S_W = beta(1-cos psi), q = ||(Hess V_t)_-||
python: numpy 2.4.6 / scipy -- single process, deterministic

Reading of the object: q(t) is DIMENSIONLESS (pure-number action, dimensionless
group coordinates).  t is the group heat-kernel time in the unit-round-S^3 metric.
Hence Q carries one power of [t] and e^{-2Q} presupposes a normalisation t_* = 1/lam_1.

